arguments.prompt:
Explore the Microsoft.Agents.AI NuGet package API surface to understand how to use it. Look at the assemblies in the NuGet cache.

1. Find the Microsoft.Agents.AI and Microsoft.Agents.AI.Abstractions DLLs in ~/.nuget/packages
2. Use `dotnet run` or reflection to list key types - specifically look for:
   - ChatClientAgent or AgentWorker or similar agent classes
   - AgentInvokeOptions or similar options classes
   - Any tool-related attributes or classes
   - How to invoke an agent (InvokeAsync, InvokeStreamingAsync, etc.)

Run these commands:
```
find ~/.nuget/packages/microsoft.agents.ai -name "*.dll" | head -5
find ~/.nuget/packages/microsoft.agents.ai.abstractions -name "*.dll" | head -5
```

Then for each found DLL, list the public types:
```
dotnet new console -n TempExplore -o /tmp/temp-explore --force
cd /tmp/temp-explore
# Write a quick program that loads the assembly and lists types
cat > Program.cs << 'EOF'
using System.Reflection;
var paths = new[] {
    Directory.GetFiles(Path.Combine(Environment.GetFolderPath(Environment.SpecialFolder.UserProfile), ".nuget/packages/microsoft.agents.ai"), "Microsoft.Agents.AI.dll", SearchOption.AllDirectories).FirstOrDefault(),
    Directory.GetFiles(Path.Combine(Environment.GetFolderPath(Environment.SpecialFolder.UserProfile), ".nuget/packages/microsoft.agents.ai.abstractions"), "Microsoft.Agents.AI.Abstractions.dll", SearchOption.AllDirectories).FirstOrDefault()
};
foreach (var p in paths.Where(p => p != null))
{
    Console.WriteLine($"\n=== {Path.GetFileName(p)} ===");
    var asm = Assembly.LoadFrom(p!);
    foreach (var t in asm.GetExportedTypes().OrderBy(t => t.FullName))
    {
        var kind = t.IsInterface ? "interface" : t.IsAbstract ? "abstract" : t.IsEnum ? "enum" : "class";
        Console.WriteLine($"  [{kind}] {t.FullName}");
        foreach (var m in t.GetMethods(BindingFlags.Public | BindingFlags.Instance | BindingFlags.DeclaredOnly).Where(m => !m.IsSpecialName))
            Console.WriteLine($"    method: {m.Name}({string.Join(", ", m.GetParameters().Select(p2 => $"{p2.ParameterType.Name} {p2.Name}"))})");
        foreach (var prop in t.GetProperties(BindingFlags.Public | BindingFlags.Instance | BindingFlags.DeclaredOnly))
            Console.WriteLine($"    prop: {prop.PropertyType.Name} {prop.Name}");
    }
}
EOF
dotnet run
```

Report all types and their key methods/properties so I know how to wire up an agent with tools.

